{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["Even though each and every commandment stands on its own, there is a kind of derash to join the sections. The sense of <b>judges</b>: even though you are obligated to go three times a year to the place of the priests, the ministers of the Temple, and there you may inquire of the statutes and the laws, this is not sufficient for you until you have judges in all your gates." "And <b>officers</b> are the rulers, from the root of שוטר and מושל, and likewise משטרו בארץ (he ruled in the land). The sense is that the judge judges and the officer enforces what is right." "<b>in all your gates.</b> And thus we find that Jehoshaphat did." "<b>for your tribes.</b> In every gate of tribe by tribe." "<b>and they shall judge the people.</b> Refers back to the judges."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:23:44.518034653Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}